UPLOADED PROPOSAL REVIEW — RIGHTS HOLDER DECISION REQUIRED

1. OWNERSHIP AND COPYRIGHT
   The uploaded file states Copyright (c) 2026 [PUBLISHER LEGAL NAME].
   Legal publisher, code/design/diagram copyright provenance and all
   contributor rights remain UNVERIFIED. Keep root all-rights-reserved
   holding notice until ownership and publication strategy are confirmed.

2. PROPOSED PERMISSIONS AND GitHub FORKING
   The upload allowed reading for evaluation and GitHub Terms-permitted
   forks solely for proposals to this repository. Any operative licence
   must be reconciled with GitHub Terms, contributor workflow and counsel;
   this comparison does not promise those permissions beyond applicable law.

3. COPYING, MODIFICATION AND COMMERCIAL REUSE
   Proposed custom prohibitions on copying/redistribution/derivatives
   and commercial/noncommercial service use require an owner-approved,
   legally enforceable grant/restriction structure. The current root
   notice is NOT an OSI-approved open-source licence.

4. NAMES, MARKS AND MODEL TRAINING
   Proposed blanket bans on Madalasa/Alarka "confusingly similar" brands,
   AI training and benchmarking cannot be assumed enforceable merely
   because source text says so. Trademark registration, ownership,
   licensing and applicable statutory limits require independent counsel.

5. HUMAN MONITORING AND CHILD DATA
   The uploaded clause prohibiting unauthorized monitoring matches the
   project's safety intent, but **software copyright permissions are not
   the legal basis to process a child's data**. Applicable India child
   data, verified guardian authority, Android OS permissions, and Google
   Play monitoring rules must be satisfied independently. Never promote
   a proposed licence clause as product/privacy regulatory approval.

6. CONTRIBUTIONS
   The uploaded draft claimed a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable,
   royalty-free contributor grant. DO NOT represent this as accepted by
   any past/current contributor. Obtain a separate approved contributor
   license/assignment process with appropriate affirmative agreement.

7. THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS
   All dependencies, screenshots, fonts, maps, trademarks and Figma
   content are governed by their actual upstream licences/terms.
   Root copyright notice cannot relicense third-party materials.

8. WARRANTY, LIABILITY AND INDIA GOVERNING LAW
   Uploaded "as is", broad liability exclusion and India law/jurisdiction
   clauses require real publisher identification and lawyer review.
   [CONFIRM JURISDICTION AND COURTS WITH COUNSEL] remains unfilled.
   No legal opinion or enforceability certification is made here.

9. CONTACT DETAILS
   Uploaded [CONTACT EMAIL] is UNSET. Do not show it to users as a
   functioning permission or security contact. Provide a verified
   identity and address before approving a publishing agreement.

RECOMMENDED OWNER ACTION
  Choose one route: proprietary/source-available licence negotiated with
  counsel; an unmodified recognized open-source text such as Apache-2.0/MIT
  with proper copyright owner; or closed/private distribution. Document
  third-party and contribution rights. Only after explicit legal/owner
  sign-off should ../LICENSE be revised.

